 Fixed/improved with the help of GPT-5.6-Sol (on ChatGPT Codex) thanks.
+
+## 196 - (Fixed/Improved) AdvCiv-SAS's short-chain irrigation replacement could leave valuable BFC bonus Farms dry for up to 191 turns (Base AdvCiv had a similar untargeted routine, which AdvCiv-SAS does not use because it conflicted with SAS improvement choice)
+
+Base AdvCiv did contain `CvUnitAI::AI_irrigateTerritory`, but it did not plan an irrigation chain toward a city plot. It scanned owned plots outside every city's workable assignment, considered only plots that could already receive irrigation from fresh water or an adjacent irrigated plot, and chose mainly by the Worker's travel distance. It could therefore extend irrigation incidentally one Farm at a time, but it did not know which dry Farm or city it was helping. AdvCiv-SAS had functionally disabled this broad routine because it could spend Worker turns creating irrigation-carrying Farms without a concrete city need and interfere with our deliberate Cottage, Workshop and Farm choices.
+
+The first AdvCiv-SAS replacement was more purposeful because it started from a dry Farm or a low-food city plot, but it was only a short local heuristic. It searched at most four plots from the target, selected a plausible connector without retaining an end-to-end route, and excluded bonus plots from its dry-Farm targets. BBAI logging exposed the clearest result in save file 450: Mayapan's Maize already had a Farm but remained dry from turn 121 through turn 312, a span of 191 turns, despite an achievable owned route to irrigation.
+
+The completed cure searches for a deterministic least-cost route across adjacent owned flat farmable plots from each actual dry BFC Farm to currently available irrigation. Farm-specific bonuses are valid targets. The Worker builds the source-side missing Farm first, then recalculates after each completed link so newly carried irrigation advances along the route toward the intended target. Existing Farms and owned flat cities can carry the route without being rebuilt. The route cost favors fewer plots and penalizes replacing Workshops, matured growth improvements and other existing improvements; bonus plots and automation-protected improvements are not used as new connectors. `SAS_WORKER_AI_IRRIGATION_CHAIN_MAX_PLOTS`, 12 by default, prevents the AI from replacing improvements across an excessive part of its empire for one target.
+
+In the confirming save-file 450 run, the route toward Mayapan's Maize advanced on turns 121, 128, 138, 149 and 160; after turn 162, the dry-Farm diagnostic stopped. Najran and Elephantine remained dry because the detailed route search confirmed that water, hills and unowned or foreign plots genuinely blocked every owned farmable route rather than because the Worker forgot an achievable chain.
+
+Save file 449 independently confirmed a long route to Camulodunum's Rice: its Farm was irrigated by turn 206 and remained so until an enemy pillaged it on turn 319. Ollantaytambo initially had no owned route, then its border expansion made one valid on turn 152 and Workers completed it by turn 176. Save file 452 produced 110 selected irrigation-chain jobs; valid routes used at most 7 plots, so none reached the default maximum of 12. The only five repeated target/location failures were explained by current ownership or terrain, and Avar's later repeated dry Farm was a pillaged improvement that Workers repaired before its diagnostic stopped again.
+
+Fixed/improved with the help of GPT-5.6-Sol (on ChatGPT Codex) thanks.

