 - **Worker mobility / overimprovement refinement:** workers still rotate away from sufficiently improved small cities, but medium and large cities are less likely to leave useful BFC plots unimproved. Workers also avoid ordinary replacement churn (e.g. **Mine ↔ Windmill**, **Cottage ↔ Farm**) while valid unimproved BFC work remains, except for bonus fixes and irrigation-chain Farms. The small-city rotation shortcut does not make a worker leave when it is already standing on this same city's useful BFC plot and that plot is the city's best current job.
 - **Finish valuable followup builds after feature removal:** a worker can complete standalone Forest/Jungle/Fallout removal (including receiving Forest chop production sooner, separated from e.g. a 2 in 1 mine that would deliver hammer on feature remove later plus would be less flexible), then continue directly into the worthwhile Mine, Farm, Cottage, resource improvement, etc. selected for that plot. This prevents workers from chopping or clearing a strong tile, walking away, and paying another trip later (which is especially inefficient if this costs movement/delay again); weak ordinary follow-ups are still reconsidered instead of being forced. Queued follow-ups now wait for the worker's next turn when removal consumes all movement rather than being silently discarded. See also [KI#176](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#176---fixed-base-advcivk-mod-mission-queue-bug-exposed-by-advciv-sas-worker-follow-up-improvements-stale-ai-worker-build-target-could-execute-on-the-wrong-plot).
