-- **Worker irrigation-chain hunting:** updated SAS AI worker logic so it now **starts from actual dry-farm / low-food BFC targets** and **hunts short owned irrigation-chain steps**, including first links **outside the city BFC**. This fixed Chaco Canyon and Harappan-style cases where a nearby (2-3 plots away from BFC) water source existed but BFC-only worker logic missed the first link. Workers now retain only the strongest available connector toward each target instead of treating several alternative routes to the same Farm as separate urgent jobs, leaving other workers free to pursue valuable improvements elsewhere.
+- **Earlier Worker irrigation-chain hunting:** AdvCiv-SAS initially improved on BFC-only Worker logic by starting from actual dry-Farm / low-food BFC targets and hunting short owned irrigation-chain steps, including first links outside the city BFC. This fixed Chaco Canyon and Harappan-style cases where a nearby water source existed 2-3 plots beyond the BFC, and retained only the strongest connector toward each target instead of treating alternative routes as separate urgent jobs. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6076+) However, this was still a short heuristic rather than a complete route planner and was later replaced by the follow-up below.
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6076+) **Workers now plan and complete long irrigation routes for dry city Farms:** BBAI logging later showed that the preceding short-chain hunt could select one nearby connector without preserving a complete route, and it excluded bonus-specific Farms. In save file 450, Mayapan's Maize consequently remained dry (i.e. not irrigated) from turn 121 through turn 312. The AI now calculates the least-cost owned route from an actual dry BFC Farm to available irrigation, builds the irrigation source-side Farm first, and recalculates after each completed link so the water advances toward the intended Farm. Owned flat cities can carry the route, while replacing valuable improvements is discouraged and excessive routes are prevented by an XML-tunable maximum. Mayapan completed its five-link route by turn 162, and save files 449 and 452 confirmed longer Farm-specific bonus routes while leaving only targets genuinely blocked by geography or foreign/unowned plots. See [KI#196](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#196---fixedimproved-advciv-sass-short-chain-irrigation-replacement-could-leave-valuable-bfc-bonus-farms-dry-for-up-to-191-turns-base-advciv-had-a-similar-untargeted-routine-which-advciv-sas-does-not-use-because-it-conflicted-with-sas-improvement-choice).
 
